---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import {
  StatePanelPlayground,
  StatePanelKinds,
  StatePanelSamples,
  StatePanelFlow,
  StatePanelCompositions,
} from '../../components/StatePanelDemo';
import {
  SamplePresetsPlayground,
  SamplePresetsGallery,
  SamplePresetsRecords,
  SamplePresetsProps,
} from '../../components/StatePanelSamplesDemo';
---

<Docs title="State Panel">
  <h1 class="docs-title">State Panel</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    One calm place for empty, loading, success, unavailable, and error states. It explains what happened and offers the
    next step.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <StatePanelPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="State panel usage"
      code={`import { StatePanel } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/state-panel";

<StatePanel
  kind="error"
  heading="h3"
  title="Could not open this file"
  description={error.message}
>
  <Button variant="outline" onClick={retry}>Try again</Button>
</StatePanel>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>kind</code> is <code>"empty"</code>, <code>"loading"</code>, <code>"success"</code>,{' '}
      <code>"unavailable"</code>, or <code>"error"</code>. Loading shows a spinner, success a check, and error a
      warning. Empty and unavailable show
      <code>icon</code>, which defaults to an inbox. Any component that takes a<code>size</code> number works, including
      your own brand glyphs. Pass
      <code>icon={null}</code> for a text-only empty or unavailable panel.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>heading</code> sets the title element, <code>h1</code> to <code>h4</code>, and defaults to <code>h2</code>.
      Use <code>h1</code> when the panel is the whole page, like a not-found route. An error panel must have children,
      so people always have a way to recover.
    </p>
    <StatePanelKinds client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Sample preview</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Empty state with a sample"
      code={`<StatePanel
  kind="empty"
  icon={Files}
  title="No files yet"
  description="Upload the documents your work depends on."
  sample={<FilesPreview />}
>
  <Button><Add aria-hidden="true" />Upload files</Button>
</StatePanel>`}
    />
    <p>
      Empty panels can take a <code>sample</code>: a picture of the page once it has content. The panel becomes a card
      that sizes to its container, not the window. The preview hides below 28rem and moves beside the text from 48rem.
      The preview is hidden from assistive technology and cannot be focused. Pass
      <code>undefined</code> to fall back to the centered layout.
    </p>
    <StatePanelSamples client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Sample presets</h2>
    <p>
      Sixteen ready-made samples ship with State Panel, one for each TulipFarm page that can be empty. Each one is a{' '}
      <a href="/components/state-sample/">State Sample</a> window with fixed, realistic content.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Sample preset usage"
      code={`import { StatePanel, WorkflowsSample } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/state-panel";

<StatePanel
  kind="empty"
  icon={BranchDown}
  title={archived ? "No archived workflows" : "No workflows yet"}
  description="Describe the work in chat, review its diagram, then save and activate it."
  sample={archived ? undefined : <WorkflowsSample />}
>
  <Button variant="outline">New workflow</Button>
</StatePanel>`}
    />
    <div class="mt-6">
      <SamplePresetsPlayground client:load />
    </div>
    <p>
      Only <code>RecordsSample</code> takes data, because it copies the table you are looking at. Every preset also
      accepts the outer window props: <code>label</code> changes the “Example” chip, and <code>className</code>,{' '}
      <code>data-*</code>, and other <code>div</code> attributes go to the window root.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Every preset</h2>
    <p>
      Each card names the export and the TulipFarm page that shows it. Avatars, brand icons, file-type icons, and badges
      come from Sprõut's <a href="/components/avatar/">Avatar</a>, <a href="/components/brand-icon/">Brand Icon</a>,{' '}
      <a href="/components/attachment/">Attachment</a>, and <a href="/components/badge/">Badge</a>.
    </p>
    <SamplePresetsGallery client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Rows preset</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Rows sample from a table definition"
      code={`<RecordsSample
  table={table.definition.label}
  fields={table.definition.fields.map((field) => field.label)}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>table</code> becomes the current crumb after “Tables”. The first three
      <code>fields</code> become columns. The first is wide and starts with a colored mark, and the rest share the
      space. With no fields, one wide “Row” column is shown. Cell values are gray bars, so the sample never shows
      made-up data.
    </p>
    <SamplePresetsRecords client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Window props and overflow</h2>
    <p>
      Presets fill their container. Long titles, crumbs, and column names truncate with an ellipsis instead of widening
      the page.
    </p>
    <SamplePresetsProps client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Changing state</h2>
    <p>
      Render the panel that matches your request. Loading and success are announced politely; errors are announced right
      away. When a retry removes the focused button, move focus to the surrounding region.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <StatePanelFlow client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="state-panel-actions">
    <h2 class="section-title">Actions</h2>
    <p>
      Children sit under the description. Use buttons, links rendered as buttons, guidance text, or an inline alert.
      Wrap several links in your own row to keep them side by side. A child that renders nothing leaves no gap.
    </p>
    <StatePanelCompositions client:load />
    <p>Requests, permissions, and routing in these examples are sample code. The package only draws the panel.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The icon tile is decorative. Error text uses <code>role="alert"</code>; loading and success text use{' '}
      <code>role="status"</code>. Match
      <code>heading</code> to the surrounding outline. Sample presets are pictures, not controls, and nothing in them
      can be focused. The panel fades in over 180ms and the spinner turns; reduced motion turns both off.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
